WEBVTT

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:39.760
In the end, the majority decided 
that Steel Lady Nanase was fiction.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.950
Sakuragawa Rikka's schemes 
have been rejected.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:24.490
Well, well...

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.860
We've received an email. 
It's from Rikka-san.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:28.980
Huh?!

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:33.250
This is Kuro-senpai's laptop, so I'm 
sure she knew his email address.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.250
Rikka

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.250
Sakuragawa Kuro

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.250
Subject    No Subject

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.250
Kuro, Kotoko-san,

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:37.760
So she knew that it was you two 
who were getting in her way.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.790
<i>I guess that makes sense.</i>

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:42.980
<i>The only one who could get in the way 
of her ability to determine the future</i>

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.260
<i>is Kuro-kun, who has the same ability.</i>

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.370
<i>And she's the only one who'd 
do something like this.</i>

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:53.230
Honestly, Rikka-san. I've asked you so many 
times not to call me by my first name.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:55.980
Do you not like "Kotoko"?

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:00.350
It's hard for me to say myself, and I 
think others have a hard time, as well.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:04.990
And because of that, it doesn't 
feel right when people say it.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.240
That's why I have Kuro-senpai 
call me by my surname.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:12.750
Oh, so that's why he calls you by your 
surname even though you're going out.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:17.290
Did you doubt that we were actually dating?

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.260
I told you that from the start.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:23.470
More importantly, 
Rikka-san said "this time."

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:27.770
I'm sure she intends to make another 
monster of the imagination.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.110
This isn't enough to dissuade her, either.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.850
Why is Rikka-san doing this?

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:38.230
People's imaginations hold an
endless amount of potential.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:41.870
They can create yokai, ghosts, and demons.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:44.700
We give life to monsters 
without even realizing it.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.990
And if that's true, then anything is possible.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.070
You might even be able to create a god.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.540
B-But that's...

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.130
That's not an answer at all.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:02.050
What's the point in creating a god?

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.650
Good work out there!

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:19.570
After dying and coming back to life so 
many times, I'm sure you're out of energy.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:23.170
You must replenish your 
nutrients at once. Eat this.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:26.310
You're the one who needs nourishment.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:32.250
You created so many 
possibilities and futures,

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.510
and had me grasp them. 
I know how much energy that takes.

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:38.400
Now, don't be like that. Just eat.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.410
I'm sure it'll put Saki-san at ease, too, 
if she sees you eating like a human.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:49.480
I only ask that I get to partake 
of your banana later, Kuro-senpai.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:53.290
Please... I'm begging you...

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:56.050
Don't make vulgar jokes like 
that at a time like this.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:59.610
Oh, blessed day! 
That accursed Steel Lady is gone!

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:22.050
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:26.330
Hooray for our lady!

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:44.690
Let's hurry back home.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.700
Aw...

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:51.690
Why not let me enjoy the 
praise a little longer?

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.210
It looks like Saki-san's about to pass out.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:02.340
I'm sorry, Saki-san.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.840
If I'd tried to stop Rikka-san earlier,

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.220
we might've been able to deal with 
this before Terada-san was killed.

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:12.070
I'm sure neither of you could have

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:14.970
predicted that something 
like this would happen.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.730
So it was out of all of our hands.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:22.600
Your ability to determine the future

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.410
isn't exactly powerful enough 
to save everyone.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.980
<i>There are very few people who believe in</i>

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:36.420
<i>and speak of the spectre
Steel Lady Nanase anymore.</i>

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:39.000
Steel Lady Nanase Wiki Site

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:38.630
<i>People's interest transferred over to</i>

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:41.910
<i>solving the mystery and finding out 
if Nanase Karin was actually alive.</i>

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.520
Steel Lady Nanase Wiki Site

