<b>Steel Lady Nanase Wiki Site Wiki

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.750
<i>The fictional tale about</i>

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:57.850
<i>Nanase Karin being alive and 
someone else dying in her place.</i>

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.020
<b>Was the one who created the Steel Lady Nanase 
Wiki Site Nanase Karin?</b>

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.020
<b>List of details regarding the Steel Lady Nanase case</b>

00:06:58.530 --> 00:06:59.710
<i>The rumors are so dramatic</i>

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.540
<b>News about Nanase Karin</b>

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.540
<b>Nanase Karin sightings</b>

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:04.120
<i>that it's hard to speak about 
them publicly in the real world.</i>

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.040
<b>Someone said they saw a girl with big boobs in West Makurazaka on 9/3. Apparently,
She was wearing a mask, despite it being summer and seemed worried being noticed.</b>

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.040
<b>Someone reported seeing someone resembling her at Makurazaka Central Park at the end of January</b>

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.040
<b>Someone saw someone resembling Nanase Karin get into a cab in front of Makurazaka Station</b>

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.520
<b>The truth behind those mysterious postings</b>

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.520
<b>Who made those mysterious posts?</b>

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.520
<b>List of posts</b>

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:08.030
<b>News about Nanase Karin

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:07.900
<i>It's as if they're from an alternative 
reality different from our own.</i>

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:12.780
<i>Almost like a story we'd see 
on TV or in the newspaper.</i>

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:17.250
<i>Which means it's unlikely
that anyone would actually</i>

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:19.790
<i>bump into anyone involved in 
Nanase Karin's case in real life.</i>

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:23.140
<i>This drama was resolved 
within the Internet.</i>

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:27.820
<i>The story would be sullied if 
anyone pursued it in reality.</i>

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.830
<i>Even if people continued to embellish 
this story and talk of it quietly,</i>

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:35.810
<i>they would still deny 
Steel Lady Nanase's existence.</i>

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.780
<i>That's how much care 
she put into all of this.</i>

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:41.580
I'm never making her my enemy...

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.370
<i>As for the police,</i>

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:53.590
<i>they apparently intend to look 
into the possibility that</i>

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.620
<i>Nanase Karin's body was someone else's,</i>

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:58.620
<i>and find out who created the site.</i>

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:01.010
<i>Even if they looked into it,</i>

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:03.710
<i>there's no proof that the body 
belonged to someone else.</i>

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:07.650
<i>I'm sure the brass will 
eventually decide that they</i>

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:09.650
<i>were just being led around by the rumors</i>

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:13.630
<i>on the Internet, and that Nanase Karin 
did indeed die in January of this year.</i>

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:19.390
<i>We won't find out what happened 
to Nanase Karin and her family.</i>

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:23.950
<i>The killer who murdered 
Detective Terada has disappeared.</i>

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:37.450
<i>Back to business as usual. This is my life.</i>

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.170
Saki-san.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:51.110
Uh, wait. Where's Iwanaga-san?

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.670
She's still asleep.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.430
Huh? But it's been a full day.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:58.940
She overworked her brain 
all day yesterday,

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.680
so I figured this would happen.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.260
You should act a little more concerned.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:05.950
I will, when it's necessary.

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.440
You wanted to know about Rikka-san, right?

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.830
Yes. What is she after?

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:15.170
I asked Iwanaga-san, but she 
just changed the subject.

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:21.410
I've resigned myself to the fact that 
I have this body and this ability.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:27.350
For now, it seems that I'm still 
growing and aging normally,

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:29.420
so while I can't die from 
an accident or injury,

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:34.170
I'm hopeful that I can still die of old age.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:38.000
I can't use my ability to 
determine the future unless I die,

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:41.680
but I'm not usually in situations 
dangerous enough to kill me,

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:45.140
so I think I'll be able to live a normal life.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:48.020
<i>Normal... Normal, huh?</i>

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.650
But that's not the case for Rikka-san.

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:52.630
She's trying to use her 
ability as much as she can

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:55.240
to return to being a normal human being.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.200
Is that even possible?

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:02.580
Even if she used her ability to 
go through all the possibilities...

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.700
A future where she's a normal human being?

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.340
How could such a miracle happen?

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:11.460
<i>That's right. Rikka-san was 
at the university hospital</i>

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:15.630
<i>trying to find out if it was medically 
possible to return her back to normal.</i>

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:21.720
<i>In the end, there were no possibilities 
based on logical methods.</i>

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.810
<i>She decided she'd have to grasp 
the future she wanted herself.</i>

00:10:26.410 --> 00:10:28.480
<i>And then what happened?</i>

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:32.650
People's imaginations might 
even be able to create a god.

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:37.140
So Rikka-san is trying to create 
a monster of the imagination

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:40.200
that possesses the ability to turn 
her back into a normal human being...

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:45.160
She's trying to create something 
that has godly powers like that?

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:47.830
I'm quite certain that Rikka-san

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.710
will do whatever it takes.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:54.340
I don't know what she's thinking.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:58.660
She wants to be normal, 
but does the most abnormal things.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:03.600
Even before she consumed the 
flesh of the kudan and mermaid,

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:08.460
I can't help but think that she may 
have always been a monster at heart.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:14.480
But Kuro-kun, you still 
love Rikka-san, don't you?

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.230
I can't shake that, either.

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:18.740
So what will you do now?

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:22.500
Rikka-san's going to continue 
trying to make a monster, right?

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:24.980
Iwanaga won't let that happen.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.180
No matter what the reason may be,

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:31.670
a person or monster trying to create 
a monster for their own desires

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:33.380
goes against the natural order.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:38.830
That's basically why she gave 
up her right eye and left leg.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:44.140
So I guess you're not going 
to let it slide either, then.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:47.140
As much as I hate to say it...

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.530
Did you delete my number 
from your phone?

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:55.590
Yes.

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:57.610
Iwanaga kept nagging me about it.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.690
Even if she didn't nag, 
you can't keep my number.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:01.740
She's the type who'd 
let that bother her.

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:04.870
Yes, but...

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:08.490
It's not like we could ever 
start over again, Saki-san.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:14.000
Yeah. Seeing you after all this time 
just confirmed that it's impossible.

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:18.230
I'm okay with sitting 
across the table from you,

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:21.190
but I'd be a bit hesitant to touch you.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:22.720
I'm sorry.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:26.970
No, it's also my fault 
for keeping it a secret.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:31.220
Make sure you take care of Iwanaga-san.

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:32.680
I do.

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:36.410
She's always been oblivious of danger.

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:40.190
In a way, she's more fearless than I am.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.150
She's been hurt more than a few times

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:45.950
while trying to resolve 
conflicts between monsters.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:52.200
To be honest, I didn't want to involve 
Iwanaga in the matter with Rikka-san.

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:56.210
I was trying to take care of 
it before she got involved.

00:12:57.570 --> 00:13:03.130
But after this incident, Rikka-san realizes 
that Iwanaga is the biggest obstacle

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:05.140
that stands in her way.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:10.260
Which means that Rikka-san 
might go after Iwanaga next.

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:13.980
<i>That never even crossed my mind...</i>

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:16.780
<i>Considering what Rikka-san is capable of,</i>

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:18.910
<i>if she thinks Iwanaga-san is in her way...</i>

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:23.940
So that's why you were looking for 
Rikka-san without telling Iwanaga-san?

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.140
Though I'm sure if you had told her,

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:28.790
Iwanaga-san would've tried to get involved.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.450
I won't let Iwanaga die.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:33.700
Because she's someone who 
deserves to be happy.

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:39.170
<i>Now I can finally get some closure.</i>

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:42.470
<i>I'm pretty sure I'll never see him again.</i>

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:47.910
Are you sure I can have this bike?

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.630
Iwanaga bought this so she 
could travel around the city.

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:55.430
It'd be a pain to take it back home, 
so Iwanaga wanted you to have it.

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:58.100
Oh, and she told the monsters

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:02.030
around the city not to appear 
in front of you anymore.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.270
Thanks...

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:05.860
<i>Not sure if that makes 
me feel any better...</i>

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:09.630
See you!

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:25.590
<i>I still get scared at night.</i>

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:35.390
<i>But...</i>

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:40.480
<i>There's someone out there 
protecting the order of things.</i>

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:45.530
<i>I'm sure the world won't end 
up a crazy mess after all.</i>

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:03.040
<b>She Who Defends Order</b>

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.050
<i>I messed up again!</i>

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:07.550
<i>I keep messing up over and over again!</i>

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.550
<i>I slept for a day and a half...</i>

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:13.220
Oh, it's still only six.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:16.000
I feel quite refreshed, for only 
sleeping about four hours...

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:17.680
<b>9/6 (Tues)</b>

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.680
September 6th?

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.330
I was completely knocked 
out for 28 hours?!

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:26.300
<i>I gave Kuro-senpai and Saki-san so 
much time to spend alone together!</i>

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.930
<i>This is the biggest mistake of my life!</i>

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:35.850
Iwanaga?

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:38.620
Huh, she's not here?

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:39.870
Senpai!

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:42.420
Ow! Ow!

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:44.330
Oh, she's just in the bath.

00:15:46.810 --> 00:15:48.410
Take your time in there.

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:53.300
If you're still tired, we can 
probably stay another ni—

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:00.150
You reek of Saki-san!

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:01.580
That's impossible.

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:03.410
But I know you saw her!

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:07.400
Yeah, because you said you 
wanted to give her the bicycle.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:09.930
So I thought the sooner the better.

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:11.370
And I had some time on my hands.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:13.420
Well, yes, I did, but...

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:14.910
How did you get her contact info?

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:19.470
On the way back in the car the other 
night, we exchanged numbers...

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:23.210
But I already deleted her number.

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.380
I won't be seeing Saki-san again.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.370
That's not the problem here!

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:30.880
You need to dry off first. 
You're going to catch a cold.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:36.050
Wait! What are you doing?!

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:38.930
I don't have another clean shirt!

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:41.370
This isn't funny!

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:42.890
Just give in!

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:48.850
Thanks for everything.

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:51.020
Thank you for staying with us.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:57.890
You're still mad?

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:00.940
I'm not. I'm just reflecting.

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:05.300
I should've woken up after 12 hours.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:08.330
I'm going to work on increasing 
my strength and vitality.

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:19.220
Should we take a taxi?

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:22.170
The station isn't that far. Let's just walk.

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:25.230
It looks like it's going to rain.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:26.730
<b>For
Pedestrians
and
Bicycles</b>

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:29.310
Am I going to have to sit around on 
a bench with you as you nap again?

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:34.190
Even I couldn't possibly doze 
off after sleeping for 28 hours!

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:37.950
Senpai.

00:17:38.930 --> 00:17:42.700
I'm sure Rikka-san won't make 
her next move immediately,

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:45.890
but I'm going to tell all of the yokai 
and monsters across the country

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:48.460
to let me know if they see anything.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:52.550
I'd rather not go through 
all that trouble again.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:56.090
The best way to take care of this is 
to find her and talk to her in person.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:18:01.470
Also, if you find out anything new, 
please don't act without telling me.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:02.970
I'll see what I can do.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.650
Honestly...

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:05.670
Iwanaga...

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:10.360
If you know about the Kuebiko, 
then you also know about Princess Iwanaga.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:12.230
Yes, from the <i>Kojiki</i>.

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:16.370
It sounds just like my surname, 
so of course I know about it.

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:18.940
Princess Iwanaga.

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:21.920
The older sister of 
Princess Konohana-no-Sakuya.

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:24.190
They were both given in 
marriage to Ninigi-no-Mikoto,

00:18:24.190 --> 00:18:26.620
descendant of the high god.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:30.840
But Ninigi-no-Mikoto only married 
Princess Konohana-no-Sakuya

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.430
and sent Princess Iwanaga back home.

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:38.000
That enraged their father, Oyamatsumi.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:41.890
There was a reason I 
gave you both sisters!

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.670
Just as the "iwa," or "rock," 
in Princess Iwanaga's name suggests,

00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:48.290
she was able to give life as eternal as rocks

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:51.400
that never change month to 
month, year after year.

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:55.910
But because Ninigi-no-Mikoto didn't 
marry her and returned her to her father,

00:18:56.520 --> 00:19:01.030
he and his progeny were granted short 
lives that scattered like flowers on trees.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:04.030
They became mortal.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:06.160
Then you get it, right?

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.990
I'm immortal, so I don't belong

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:10.790
with Princess Konohana-no-Sakuya.

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:13.750
I need Princess Iwanaga.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:21.130
I'm sure you thought that was smooth,

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:25.390
but you know why Princess Iwanaga 
was returned home, don't you?

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.140
Let's not worry about the minor details.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:29.830
It's not minor at all!

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:33.480
Princess Iwanaga was sent home 
because she was ugly!

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:37.390
You couldn't have used a 
worse metaphor for a girl!

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:43.590
But you're prettier than any flower, 
so I haven't sent you back anywhere.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.180
Either way,

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:11.310
it's never good to judge anyone 
by their physical appearance.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:15.760
You're just an amalgamation 
of a mermaid and a kudan.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:17.750
Stop trying to sound like you're so cool.

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:37.430
Senpai, will you be staying 
at my place tonight?

00:20:37.430 --> 00:20:39.090
My parents have been wanting to see you.

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:43.740
Well, I do need to apologize 
for putting them out.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:45.920
There's no need to be so formal.

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:48.720
You can think of them and 
our house as your own.

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:50.050
I can't.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:53.230
I can't let you fence me in just yet.

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:56.980
Do you still think you 
can get away from me?

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:11.870
<i>In this world, there are yokai, ayakashi,</i>

00:21:12.280 --> 00:21:13.870
<i>spectres, demons,</i>

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:16.870
<i>mononoke, and ghosts.</i>

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:19.960
<i>Creatures with those names exist, 
just like everything else.</i>

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:26.900
<i>There is reason that transcends reason,</i>

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:29.140
<i>and logical and illogical go hand in hand.</i>

00:21:31.070 --> 00:21:33.650
<i>But there's no reason to be afraid.</i>

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:36.140
<i>There is an order to all things.</i>

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:40.400
<i>No matter what methods 
Rikka-san tries to use,</i>

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:44.890
<i>no matter how much she 
wants to create a new god,</i>

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:48.570
<i>I will protect that order, regardless.</i>

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:52.080
<i>Even if I have to create a rational fiction...</i>

00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:55.050
<i>or a fiction that transcends the truth.</i>

00:21:56.150 --> 00:21:59.500
<i>I will defend this world from that 
gap between truth and fiction.</i>

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:02.730
Kuro-senpai.

00:22:04.450 --> 00:22:07.950
I believe today will be a lovely day.

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:16.080
<b>The End</b>
